 "name": "Offensive Infinity",
 "type": "spell",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/limitless.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Limitless — Innate Technique (11th level)</em></p><p>At 11th level, you have learned to push infinity to an aggressive mode through offensive training. As an action, you can spend CE up to your Cursed Energy modifier to amplify <em>Infinity</em>. All creatures within 10 ft must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, they are forced 10 ft directly away from you and take 2d8 force damage per cursed energy spent. On a successful save they take half as much damage and are not pushed away. <br />\nIf used at <em>Maximum Output</em>, a creature within 5 ft makes this save at disadvantage.<br />\n Alternatively, you can choose one target within 5 ft of you and 10 ft away from a wall or solid structure, and spend CE up to your CE modifier as an action to crush them against it. The target must make a Strength saving throw, being forced against the wall and taking 3d8 Force damage for each Cursed Energy spent and be restrained until the start of your next turn on a failed save. On a success, they are pushed 5 ft back and take half as much damage. If you are more than 10 ft away from the target, the technique ends.<br />\n If used at <em>Maximum Output</em>, you can spend CE up to your modifier at the start of your turn to maintain the technique, forcing the creature to repeat the save.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
